+name: Conditional checkbox desync — check then uncheck submits clean (optional path)
+description: |
+  The conditional-checkbox state round-trip drive for the OPTIONAL guarantor
+  path (2026-08-04 final policy: employed/self-employed renters and retired
+  applicants keep the plain optional checkbox — it must round-trip like
+  every other field and NEVER self-mark; the required cohorts' declared
+  treatment is pinned by the missing-guarantor-when-* and
+  stepper/guarantor-required-at-step scenarios).
+
+  With `checkbox_desync_flow: true`:
+
+  1. Fill the whole long form (stepper=off) as an EMPLOYED RENTER
+     (never_rented_before unticked, landlord-ref trio, employer trio) per
+     form_data, but with employer_ref_name deliberately EMPTY to force an
+     error re-render. (Do NOT try a malformed ref email — ref trios are
+     only non-empty-validated server-side, verified in browser 2026-08-04.)
+  2. CHECK [name="has_guarantor"] — assert the guarantor fields block
+     ([data-testid="guarantor-fields"]) becomes visible. Type a name into
+     guarantor_name (a trace value the hide must clear).
+  3. UNCHECK [name="has_guarantor"] — assert the block hides and
+     guarantor_name is cleared (form.js clearInputsWithin).
+  4. Submit (after the anti-fraud delay). Expect [data-testid="error-summary"]
+     with an employer_ref_name row — and assert the desync class stays dead:
+     a. NO error-summary row points at any guarantor field:
+        eval `document.querySelectorAll('[data-testid="error-summary"] a[href^="#field-guarantor"]').length === 0`
+     b. The checkbox did NOT self-mark on the re-render:
+        eval `document.querySelector('[name="has_guarantor"]').checked === false`
+     c. The guarantor block stayed hidden and the trace value stayed cleared:
+        eval `document.querySelector('[data-testid="guarantor-fields"]').hidden === true`
+  5. Fix employer_ref_name (fill it), RE-UPLOAD both documents (file
+     inputs do not survive the error re-render) and RE-TICK the GDPR
+     consent (never restored on re-render by design — the submit button
+     stays disabled without it), then submit again. Expect
+     [data-testid="confirmation-page"] — optional cohort + unchecked
+     guarantor is VALID.
+
+  Sibling coverage: co_applicant[N][has_guarantor] follows the identical
+  round-trip — exercised by happy-path/coapplicant-with-guarantor.
