+---
+title: 'Guarantor required-cohort UX coherence (declared-required, no self-marking)'
+type: 'bugfix'
+created: '2026-08-04'
+status: 'in-progress'
+baseline_commit: 'b25b19c9d02d8106f2f2c279bbfbe708501812f1'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — rewritten under the human-renegotiation doctrine for the 2026-08-04 rulings (see Spec Change Log)">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** On `/apply/:code`, a first-time renter who never checks "I have a guarantor" submitted and got 6 guarantor validation errors, with the re-render painting the box checked FOR them — the requirement was real but invisible until it bit (user-reported, screenshot-verified). Root cause: three silent state mechanisms — `form.js autoTickGuarantor` (auto-checked the box when never_rented_before ticked), `validate_form`'s `force_required` (server treated the box as ticked for first-time renters), and the view's `has_guarantor_default_check` (pre-ticked on re-render for never-renters/students/unemployed/retired) — each overrode the applicant's actual checkbox state with no explanation.
+
+**Approach (2026-08-04 final policy ruling):** KEEP and EXTEND the business rule — `guarantor_required = never_rented_before OR employment_status ∈ {student, unemployed}` — and fix the UX incoherence: required cohorts get DECLARED-required treatment (point-of-selection inline notes at the moment of the triggering choice; per-cohort required notices on the Guarantor step; fields auto-expanded with NO optional-checkbox gate; stepper step-level gating blocks empty fields AT THE STEP). KILL all silent state mechanisms for ALL cohorts — nothing is ever pre-ticked, anywhere; the checkbox means what the applicant last did. Retired = OPTIONAL with an honest recommendation hint. Employed/self-employed renters = plain optional path (round-trip fidelity preserved: posted-checked re-renders checked).
+
+**Product-decision line (SUPERSEDED readings, for the record):** the first implementation pass read the briefing as "retire the force rule entirely" — SUPERSEDED by the Option A ruling (keep the rule, fix UX) and then by the 2026-08-04 final policy (extend the rule to student/unemployed, retired optional, point-of-selection signalling, copy doctrine). This spec implements the final policy.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Nothing is ever pre-ticked, for any cohort — no JS auto-tick, no view default-check.
+- Required cohorts: notice + auto-expanded fields + step-level block; server `force_required` stays the no-JS backstop.
+- Validation, persistence (insert null-out), and the GDPR guarantor_attestation consent record key off ONE rule (`application_handler.guarantor_required`) — required cohorts post no checkbox flag, so persistence/consent must align or validated guarantor data is silently NULLED (found desync — see Design Notes).
+- Optional path: checkbox round-trips like every other field (checked+empty → 6 errors + re-render keeps checked; unchecked → valid).
+- Copy doctrine: definition-based guarantor framing, "usually a parent" banned everywhere (expat incoherence); checklist line uniform across prep block + invite + auto-reply + reminders; notes are honest-conditionals (appear exactly on the trigger, disappear when unmade).
+- Real-browser (Chromium, mobile viewport) evidence of all three trigger moments + the step block + the optional paths.
+
+**Ask First:** none — rulings are explicit; parked questions go in the PR body, not the code.
+
+**Never:**
+- No pre-ticking mechanism under any name (not even "advisory").
+- No requirement for retired applicants (hint only) or co-applicant guarantor cohorts (unchanged, optional).
+- No change to never_rented_before's legitimate conditional validations (character-ref swap, eviction gating) or gdpr_consent (never restored by design).
+- No merge-style draft writes; no staging/production E2E.
+- Location-based guarantor rules (Ireland-vs-foreign acceptance is PARKED — form stays location-neutral).
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+{never_rented T/F} × {student, unemployed, retired, employed, self-employed} × {guarantor present/absent}:
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| REQUIRED_ABSENT | any required cohort, guarantor fields empty | step-level block (stepper) / requirement statement + 6 field errors (submit); notice visible; box NOT pre-ticked | per-field inline errors + banner leads with the requirement row |
+| REQUIRED_PRESENT | any required cohort, fields filled, no box posted | submits clean; row persists has_guarantor=true + fields; attestation record writes | N/A |
+| OPTIONAL_ABSENT | retired/employed renter, box unticked | clean submit | N/A |
+| OPTIONAL_PRESENT_EMPTY | optional, box ticked, fields empty | 6 field errors; re-render keeps box checked + partial values | per-field inline errors |
+| OPTIONAL_UNCHECK_RERENDER | optional, box unticked, unrelated error | re-render paints box UNCHECKED (no self-marking) | unrelated error only |
+| RETIRED_HINT | retired, not first-rental | hint visible, box optional and unticked | N/A |
+| COHORT_PRECEDENCE | never_rented + student/retired | first_rental cohort wins (one notice) | N/A |
+| POINT_OF_SELECTION | tick never_rented / pick student / pick unemployed | inline note appears at that moment; unmaking the choice hides it | N/A |
+| CHECKLIST_UNIFORM | prep block / invite / auto-reply / reminders | same guarantor line everywhere; "usually a parent" absent | N/A |
+| NO_JS_REQUIRED | JS off, required cohort | long form shows fields + all notices (honest-conditional phrasing); force fires on empty submit | 6 field errors |
+| COAP_GUARANTOR | co_applicant[N][has_guarantor] check→uncheck | optional round-trip (unchanged — already correct) | N/A |
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
