+- 2026-08-04 (human addition — point-of-selection): inline notes at the moment of the triggering choice (never_rented tick on References; student/unemployed pick on Work & Income); W1a doctrine extension — uniform guarantor checklist line on invite + auto-reply + prep block; honest-conditionals both ways; real-browser evidence of all three trigger moments. Amended: Intent, Matrix, Code Map, Tasks.
+- 2026-08-04 (human copy amendment): "usually a parent" banned everywhere (expat incoherence) — definition-based framing; Ireland-vs-foreign guarantor acceptance PARKED for the PR body (form stays location-neutral). Amended: copy constants, checklist line, pins.
+- 2026-08-04 (final policy, enforcement pass): submit-time errors MUST state the requirement — banner leads with a per-cohort requirement row (user-pinned first-rental copy "A guarantor is required — first-time renters need one to back the application"; student/unemployed mirror per-cohort) whenever a required cohort submits with missing guarantor fields; the 6 field errors still fire below it. Amended: Matrix REQUIRED_ABSENT, Code Map, Tasks. (Also: the desync scenario's malformed-ref-email forcing trick corrected — ref trios are only non-empty-validated server-side, verified in browser.)
+
+## Design Notes
+
+**The found desync (evidence for the class-audit report):** the DRAFT layer is clean — `upsert_application_draft.sql` replaces fields wholesale and `form_draft.js serializeForm` omits unchecked checkboxes, so the round-trip has no merge-stale bug. The REAL desync is validation-vs-persistence: a required-cohort applicant posts full guarantor fields with NO checkbox flag (their path renders no checkbox — and on old develop, a no-JS first-timer never got the auto-tick); validation passes via force_required, then `insert_application_row`'s null-out keyed off the raw checkbox and NULLED all six fields — the landlord would see a validated-but-guarantorless application. Fixed by keying validation, null-out, and the attestation consent record off the same `guarantor_required` rule, pinned by `apply_submission_persists_guarantor_for_required_cohort_without_checkbox_test`.
+
+**Why synthetic hidden inputs:** the data-condition engine keys ONE trigger per element; the required rule is compound (never_rented OR status). Three `_guarantor_*` synthetics (SSR-stamped, JS-converged, underscore-prefixed so drafts/submits ignore them) let the declarative engine do all visibility without an engine extension. The cohort module sits BEFORE the condition engine in form.js so init converge beats the first apply().
