+// Guarantor cohort module (2026-08-04 final policy ruling).
+// Required cohorts — first-time renters, students, unemployed — get the
+// DECLARED-required Guarantor step: per-cohort notice, fields auto-expanded,
+// NO optional-checkbox gate, and nothing ever pre-ticked. Retired is
+// optional with a recommendation hint; employed/self-employed renters are
+// plain optional. The server enforces the same rule
+// (application_handler.guarantor_required).
+//
+// The form's data-condition engine keys one trigger per element, so this
+// module maintains three synthetic hidden inputs (underscore-prefixed:
+// never drafted, never persisted, ignored by the submit parser):
+//   _guarantor_cohort      "" | first_rental | student | unemployed | retired
+//   _guarantor_required    "on" | ""   (required cohorts only)
+//   _guarantor_fields_open "on" | ""   (required OR the box is ticked)
+// SSR stamps them from posted/restored values; this module recomputes them
+// from the source controls (never_rented_before, employment_status,
+// has_guarantor) and dispatches change on a flip so the engine re-applies.
+//
